# Problem Statement


Write a C++ program to represent a file directory structure using a tree data structure. The program 
should allow the user to create directories and subdirectories under a specified directory.
It should also display all subdirectories under a selected directory.
Each directory is represented as a node in the tree, and the parent-child relationship 
represents the directory hierarchy. The program demonstrates the practical application of tree data 
structures in file systems.


Modified Problem Statement

Write a C++ program to represent a file directory structure using a tree data structure. 
The program should allow users to create and remove directories, search for a directory by 
name and display its complete path, display all subdirectories under a specified directory, 
count subdirectories, and calculate the maximum depth of the directory tree.
Each directory is represented as a node in the tree, and the parent-child relationship 
represents the directory hierarchy. The program demonstrates the practical application of 
tree data structures in file management systems.
